# Automation operations: node details, unsaved-graph validation, versions, archiving,
# enrollments (enroll, pause, resume, cancel, run now), events and the dispatcher.

@token = PASTE-AN-ADMIN-DEV-TOKEN
@workflowId = PASTE-A-WORKFLOW-ID
@contactId = PASTE-A-CONTACT-ID
@officeId = PASTE-AN-OFFICE-ID

### One node type: config JSON Schema (what the canvas renders as a form) and handles
GET {{baseUrl}}/automation/nodes/branch_on_reply_bucket
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Validate a graph without saving it (live validation on the canvas)
POST {{baseUrl}}/automation/workflows/validate-graph
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"graph": {"trigger": {"id": "t", "type": "trigger_manual_enroll", "config": {}}, "nodes": [{"id": "s1", "type": "send_email", "config": {"office_id": "{{officeId}}", "template_key": "intro"}}, {"id": "s2", "type": "send_email", "config": {"office_id": "{{officeId}}", "template_key": "follow_up_1"}}], "edges": [{"source": "t", "target": "s1"}, {"source": "s1", "target": "s2"}]}}

### One workflow (current and latest version)
GET {{baseUrl}}/automation/workflows/{{workflowId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One stored version (immutable)
GET {{baseUrl}}/automation/workflows/{{workflowId}}/versions/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Archive (no new enrollments; open ones stop)
POST {{baseUrl}}/automation/workflows/{{workflowId}}/archive
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: archive-1

### Enroll contacts in a published workflow
# @name enrolled
POST {{baseUrl}}/automation/workflows/{{workflowId}}/enrollments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: enroll-1

{"contact_ids": ["{{contactId}}"]}

### One enrollment (status, next run, variables such as reply/lead/draft)
GET {{baseUrl}}/automation/enrollments/{{enrolled.response.body.0.enrollment_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Pause it
POST {{baseUrl}}/automation/enrollments/{{enrolled.response.body.0.enrollment_id}}/pause
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: pause-1

### Resume it
POST {{baseUrl}}/automation/enrollments/{{enrolled.response.body.0.enrollment_id}}/resume
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: resume-1

### Run it now (dev/staging: advance without waiting for the dispatcher)
POST {{baseUrl}}/automation/enrollments/{{enrolled.response.body.0.enrollment_id}}/advance
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Cancel it
POST {{baseUrl}}/automation/enrollments/{{enrolled.response.body.0.enrollment_id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: cancel-1

### Publish a custom event (for example from a CRM integration)
POST {{baseUrl}}/automation/events
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"type": "contact.tag_added", "contact_id": "{{contactId}}", "payload": {"tag": "intro"}, "idempotency_key": "crm-sync-42"}

### Events and what they started
GET {{baseUrl}}/automation/events?contact_id={{contactId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Run the dispatcher now for this tenant (admin; normally every 30 s on Celery beat)
POST {{baseUrl}}/automation/dispatch
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Custom event from a CRM or website form (an API key with events:write works too).
# Starts workflows whose trigger is "Custom event" with event name `quote_requested`;
# the other simple values become enrollment variables (enrollment.variables.lane).
POST {{baseUrl}}/automation/events
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: web-quote-001

{
  "type": "custom.event",
  "contact_email": "buyer@importer.example",
  "payload": {"name": "quote_requested", "lane": "YYZ-IST", "mode": "air"}
}
